# Monarch UI rules

This app builds its UI with Monarch (`@rookcom/monarch-react`,
`@rookcom/monarch-tokens`). Full rules: `AGENTS.md` in the app root.

## Find components

- Manifest: `node_modules/@rookcom/monarch-react/dist/manifest.json`. Copy the
  `import` and `css` fields of an export exactly.
- Docs: `https://monarchui.dev/components/<id>/` (Markdown at `index.md`),
  `https://monarchui.dev/llms.txt`.
- `npx monarch search <query>`, `npx monarch add <Component>`.

## Rules

1. Use a Monarch component before writing a new UI primitive. Never copy
   Monarch source into the app.
2. Avoid exports marked `scope: "rook"` (the `@rookcom/monarch-react/rook`
   entry) unless this is a Rook product.
3. Colour only through `--mn-*` tokens or `bg-mn-*`, `text-mn-*`,
   `border-mn-*` classes. No `bg-red-500`, hex, `rgb()` or `[...]` colours.
4. Type and spacing use the named scale (`text-sm`, `p-4`, `gap-2`).
5. `danger`, `success`, `warning`, `info` mean status; `accent` is the brand.
6. Icon-only controls have a label, inputs sit in a `Field` with a
   `FieldLabel`, every `Dialog` has a `DialogTitle`, destructive actions use
   `variant="danger"` and a confirmation.
7. No `window.confirm`, `alert` or `prompt`: use `useConfirm()`,
   `usePrompt()`, `useChoice()` or `useUndoToast()`.
8. With `styles/core.css`, load each stylesheet in the export's `css` field
   once in the root layout.
9. Style through props, tokens and the root and part `mn-*` classes in the
   manifest (`className`). Never target modifier classes or `--_*`
   variables.
10. Monarch does not use sparkle icons for AI; use the lucide `Bot` icon.

Outside Rook, use the neutral accent
(`@rookcom/monarch-tokens/css/products/neutral` and
`<html data-mn-product="neutral">`) or your own via `deriveTheme(hex)`.

Run `npx monarch check` before finishing and fix new findings, along with
anything the Monarch ESLint plugin (`monarch/*` rules) reports.
